  "notes": "USAGE:\n{諭|さと}す implies patient, gentle guidance from someone with more experience or authority. The person being counseled is marked with を. It conveys warmth and concern for the other person's well-being, unlike {叱|しか}る (to scold), which is harsher.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {優|やさ}しく{諭|さと}す: to gently counsel\n- {言|い}い{聞|き}かせるように{諭|さと}す: to reason with someone as if explaining\n- {子|こ}どもを{諭|さと}す: to talk sense into a child\n- {切々|せつせつ}と{諭|さと}す: to earnestly reason with\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{叱|しか}る (to scold) involves anger or firmness. {諫|いさ}める (to remonstrate) is used for advising someone of higher status against a wrong course. {諭|さと}す is gentler than both, emphasizing patient explanation and guidance.",
